# Inputs Section

## Purpose

Defines the Inputs section of the MAM specification. The section acts as a contract between the module and its consumers and specifies what data the module expects to receive.

## Inputs

| Name | Type | Required | Description |
|------|------|----------|-------------|
| content | string | Yes | Full MAM module text that contains the section |
| inputs | list | No | Input definitions to validate directly |

## Outputs

| Name | Type | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| inputs | list | Extracted input parameter definitions |
| valid | bool | Whether the section passes validation |
| errors | list | Validation errors found in the inputs |

## Capabilities

### validate

Checks table format, columns, types, names, and required values.

### extract

Pulls the input definitions out of the section table.

### document

Renders the inputs into a documentation fragment.

## Rules

- Use a Markdown table format.
- Include the Name, Type, Required, and Description columns.
- Use valid type names from the type reference.
- Mark required values as Yes or No.
- Give each parameter a unique name.
- Use snake case for parameter names.
- Document every parameter with a description.

## Workflow

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Content] --> B[Validate Table]
    B --> C[Extract]
    C --> D[Document]
    D --> E[Output]
```

## Python

```python
import re

VALID_TYPES = {"string", "int", "float", "bool", "dict", "list",
               "object", "any", "null", "file", "datetime", "json", "bytes"}

def validate_type(type_name: str) -> bool:
    return type_name in VALID_TYPES

def validate_name(name: str) -> bool:
    return bool(re.match(r"^[a-z][a-z0-9_]*$", name))

def validate_required(value: str) -> bool:
    return value in ("Yes", "No")

def extract_inputs(content: str) -> list:
    inputs = []
    in_table = False
    for line in content.split("\n"):
        if line.strip().startswith("| Name"):
            in_table = True
            continue
        if in_table and line.strip().startswith("|"):
            if "---" in line:
                continue
            parts = [p.strip() for p in line.split("|")[1:-1]]
            if len(parts) >= 4:
                inputs.append({
                    "name": parts[0],
                    "type": parts[1],
                    "required": parts[2] == "Yes",
                    "description": parts[3],
                })
        elif in_table:
            in_table = False
    return inputs

def validate_inputs(inputs: list) -> list:
    errors = []
    for item in inputs:
        if not validate_name(item["name"]):
            errors.append("Invalid name: " + item["name"])
        if not validate_type(item["type"]):
            errors.append("Invalid type: " + item["type"])
        if not isinstance(item["required"], bool):
            errors.append("Invalid required value")
    return errors

def document_inputs(inputs: list) -> str:
    docs = "## Input Parameters\n\n"
    for item in inputs:
        docs += "- " + item["name"] + " (" + item["type"] + "): " + item["description"] + "\n"
    return docs
```

## Tests

### Input

```yaml
content: |
  ## Inputs

  | Name | Type | Required | Description |
  |------|------|----------|-------------|
  | name | string | Yes | User full name |
  | email | string | Yes | User email address |
  | age | int | No | User age |
```

### Expected

```yaml
valid: true
errors: []
```

```python
def test_inputs():
    content = ("| Name | Type | Required | Description |\n"
               "|------|------|----------|-------------|\n"
               "| name | string | Yes | User full name |")
    parsed = extract_inputs(content)
    assert parsed[0]["name"] == "name"
    assert parsed[0]["required"] is True
    assert validate_name("user_name")
    assert validate_type("string")
    assert validate_inputs(parsed) == []
    assert "Input Parameters" in document_inputs(parsed)
```

## Examples

### Simple Parameters

```markdown
| Name | Type | Required | Description |
|------|------|----------|-------------|
| name | string | Yes | User full name |
| email | string | Yes | User email address |
| age | int | No | User age |
```

### File Parameters

```markdown
| Name | Type | Required | Description |
|------|------|----------|-------------|
| input_file | file | Yes | Path to input file |
| output_file | file | No | Path to output file |
| config_file | file | No | Path to configuration file |
```

